>> title: Red Enchilada Sauce
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: chiles, mexican, enchiladas, stovetop
>> servings: 6
>> time: 45 min
>> step.1: toast, soak 20 min
>> step.2: blend smooth
>> step.3: fry 10 min
>> step.4: season

Toast @dried guajillo chiles{6}(stemmed and seeded) and @dried ancho chiles{2}(stemmed and seeded) in a dry #skillet{} for ~{30%sec} a side, then soak in hot water for ~{20%min}.

Blend @&(~1)soaked chiles{} with @garlic{3%cloves}, @white onion{1/2%medium}(chopped), @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @dried Mexican oregano{1%tsp}, and @chicken stock{1 1/2%cups}(360 mL; or the chile soaking water) until smooth.

Fry @&(~1)chile purée{} in @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} over medium heat for ~{10%min}, until it darkens and thickens.

Season @&(~1)sauce{} with @kosher salt{1%tsp} and @cider vinegar{1%tsp}.
